Here is the professional-grade framework.

🎯 OBJECTIVE

Find assets that:

Have enough volatility to move

Are liquid

Are entering early trend expansion

Offer ≥ 2:1 reward:risk

Align with market regime

You are not predicting.
You are ranking probability.

🧠 STEP 1 — DETERMINE MARKET REGIME (Non-Negotiable)

Before scanning assets, classify regime.

Metrics to Compute:

Index trend (use S&P 500 proxy like SPY)

Price > 200 MA → Bull regime

Price < 200 MA → Bear regime

50 MA slope (positive or negative)

VIX level (low <18, high >25)

% of stocks above 200 MA

Why?

If regime is:

Bull → Trade long breakouts/pullbacks

Bear → Short rallies or stay defensive

Choppy → Reduce size, focus on range plays

If you skip regime filtering, your win rate collapses.

🧲 STEP 2 — UNIVERSE SELECTION

Filter tradable universe:

Market cap > $1B

Avg volume > 1M shares

Price > $10

No earnings within 5 trading days (optional)

This removes junk and gap risk.

🔥 STEP 3 — VOLATILITY FILTER

You want:

ATR% between 3.5% and 6%

Too low → no movement
Too high → unstable structure

ATR% = ATR(14) / Close

This is your “fuel” filter.

📈 STEP 4 — TREND STRENGTH FILTER

This is where edge begins.

Calculate:

Price > 20 MA

20 MA > 50 MA

50 MA slope positive

ADX(14) > 20

Higher highs / higher lows (structure check)

Optional advanced:

3-month return > S&P 500 return (relative strength filter)

Only keep stocks that pass at least 4 of 5 conditions.

This eliminates most noise.

📊 STEP 5 — VOLUME CONFIRMATION

Look for:

Volume today > 1.5x 20-day average
OR

Recent breakout with volume expansion

Volume confirms institutional participation.

No volume = weak move.

🎯 STEP 6 — ENTRY CONFIGURATION SCORING

Now score remaining assets.

A. Breakout Setup

Tight consolidation (10–20 days)

ATR contraction before expansion

Resistance clearly defined

B. Pullback Setup

Pullback to 20 or 50 MA

RSI reset to 40–50

No breakdown in structure

C. Volatility Compression Setup

Bollinger Band squeeze

Range narrowing

ADX rising from low level

Score each asset 1–5 based on:

Trend alignment

Volume expansion

Structure clarity

R:R potential

Relative strength

Rank top 5.

🧮 STEP 7 — RISK-REWARD VALIDATION

For each candidate:

Identify logical stop (below structure)

Identify logical target (previous high / measured move)

Compute R:R

Reject anything < 2:1

With $1000 account:

Risk per trade: 1%–2% max

If stop distance = $1
Risk allowed = $15
Position size = 15 shares

